<Layouts.app flash={@flash}>
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
    <div id="hero" class="hero bg-base-200 py-12 px-8 rounded-box">
      <div class="hero-content flex-col lg:flex-row gap-12">
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center text-center shrink-0">
          <div class="avatar">
            <div class="w-64 rounded-full ring ring-base-300 ring-offset-base-100 ring-offset-2 overflow-hidden">
              <img alt="me on my last year in Japan" src={~p"/images/fall_tree.jpg"} />
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-1 text-base-content/70">Bioinformatician, cloud advocate, food nerd</p>
          <div class="mt-4 flex gap-4">
            <.link
              href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jfortizq"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              aria-label="LinkedIn profile"
              class="text-base-content/80 hover:text-primary transition-colors"
            >
              <.devicon name="linkedin" class="size-8" />
            </.link>
            <.link
              href="https://github.com/biofilos"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              aria-label="GitHub profile"
              class="text-base-content/80 hover:text-primary transition-colors"
            >
              <.devicon name="github" class="size-8" />
            </.link>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="max-w-2xl">
          <h1 class="text-5xl font-bold">Nice, to meet you!</h1>
          <p class="pt-6 text-xl leading-relaxed">
            Hi, I'm Juan Felipe, a bioinformatician who loves digging into the code of life.
          </p>
          <p class="pt-4 text-xl leading-relaxed">
            Whether it's unraveling the mysteries of evolution, harnessing the power of cloud computing for genomic analysis, or experimenting with the latest data visualization techniques, I'm passionate about pushing boundaries and finding creative solutions to questions, problems, and puzzles.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section id="background">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-extrabold pt-8 pb-4">Background</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <.milestone_card
          image={~p"/images/unal_green.jpg"}
          image_alt="Jardín Botánico de San Andrés, Universidad Nacional de Colombia"
          title="BSc. Biology"
          subtitle="U. Nacional. Colombia"
        >
          As part of my thesis for Biology at the <.ext_link href="https://unal.edu.co">National University of Colombia</.ext_link>,
          I started my career working on drift algae and their taxonomy. Then I joined Manihot
          Biotec, a lab specialized in plant immunity. There, I learned about bioinformatics,
          genome annotation, molecular modelling, and phylogenetics.
        </.milestone_card>
        <.milestone_card
          image={~p"/images/laramie.jpg"}
          image_alt="At Vedawoo park"
          title="MSc. Molecular Biology"
          subtitle="U. Wyoming. USA"
        >
          For my Masters degree in Molecular Biology at the <.ext_link href="https://www.uwyo.edu">University of Wyoming</.ext_link>,
          I wrote my first program, which was used to analyze how the intrinsic protein disorder
          in flavivirus proteins has a clear phylogenetic signal.
        </.milestone_card>
        <.milestone_card
          image={~p"/images/vandy_cooking.png"}
          image_alt="Teaching how to make delicious Colombian food to my friends at the uni"
          title="PhD. Biological Sciences"
          subtitle="Vanderbilt U. USA"
        >
          In my PhD for Biological Sciences at the
          <.ext_link href="https://as.vanderbilt.edu/rokaslab/">Rokas Lab</.ext_link>
          at <.ext_link href="https://vanderbilt.edu">Vanderbilt University</.ext_link>,
          I studied how clusters of gene duplicates evolved in the mammalian phylogeny, and the
          different ways in which gene clusters improve molecular diversity, with a specific
          interest in the evolution of pregnancy and its implications in studying preterm birth
          in humans (and taught classes on Latin American food at the university).
        </.milestone_card>
        <.milestone_card
          image={~p"/images/japan.jpg"}
          image_alt="Nice garden afternoon in Osaka"
          title="SPDR Postdoctoral fellow"
          subtitle="RIKEN. Japan"
        >
          In my postdoc I moved to the <.ext_link href="https://riken.jp">RIKEN</.ext_link>
          institute in Japan. At the
          <.ext_link href="https://www.bdr.riken.jp/en/research/labs/kuraku-s/index.html">
            Laboratory for Phyloinformatics
          </.ext_link>
          at the
          <.ext_link href="https://www.bdr.riken.jp/en/index.html">
            RIKEN Center for Biosystems Dynamics Research
          </.ext_link>
          I developed computational tools to study the evolution of gene families in sharks, a
          basal vertebrate lineage. Then, as an
          <.ext_link href="https://www.riken.jp/en/careers/programs/spdr/">SPDR</.ext_link>
          recipient, I worked in the
          <.ext_link href="https://www.riken.jp/en/research/labs/ims/cell_conv/">
            Laboratory for Advanced genomics Circuit
          </.ext_link>
          at the
          <.ext_link href="https://www.riken.jp/en/research/labs/ims/">
            Center for Integrative Medical Sciences
          </.ext_link>
          at <.ext_link href="http://www.riken.jp/en">RIKEN</.ext_link>, where I developed data
          analysis and visualization applications to study chromatin dynamics in an evolutionary
          context.
        </.milestone_card>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="skills">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-extrabold pt-8 pb-4">Development Skills</h2>
      <p class="pb-6">
        During this journey, I have collected some cool tools. Check them out!
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <.skill_card
          :for={set <- @skill_sets}
          title={set.area}
          icon={set.icon}
          skills={set.skills}
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="industry">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-extrabold pt-8 pb-4">Back to the real world</h2>

      <p class="pb-6">
        After years in academia, I moved into industry, where genomics meets the real world.
      </p>
      <ol class="ms-6 flex flex-col gap-10 border-s-2 border-primary/25">
        <.timeline_item
          title="Genomic and Data Analytics Core (GEDAC)"
          icon="hero-cloud"
          badges={["Singapore"]}
          highlights={["Team leadership", "Cloud infrastructure", "Genomics at scale"]}
        >
          After my post-doctoral fellowship at
          <.ext_link href="https://www.riken.jp/en/">RIKEN</.ext_link>
          in Japan, I started my professional career as a bioinformatician and computational
          biologist. At the
          <.ext_link href="https://www.gedac.org/">Genomic and Data Analytics Core</.ext_link>
          of the <.ext_link href="https://csi.nus.edu.sg">Cancer Sciences Institute</.ext_link>
          (<.ext_link href="https://nus.edu.sg">National University of Singapore</.ext_link>),
          I led a team of scientists and software developers to build the cloud infrastructure
          the institute needed to run genomic analytical pipelines at scale, work that has made a
          positive impact in the scientific community by letting researchers easily run genomic
          workflows in a cost-effective way from an intuitive interface.
        </.timeline_item>
        <.timeline_item
          title="Senior Bioinformatics Engineer · Lifebit"
          icon="hero-briefcase"
          badges={["Singapore"]}
          highlights={["Client liaison", "Deployment & maintenance", "Stakeholder communication"]}
        >
          Then, as a Senior Bioinformatics Engineer at <.ext_link href="https://lifebit.ai">Lifebit</.ext_link>, my mission was to be the
          touch point with our clients in Singapore: communicating and developing technical
          insights to deploy and maintain the bioinformatics tools made by the company, with a
          high degree of communication between stakeholders at the client's organization and
          developers of Lifebit, to translate the needs of the clients into technical and
          scientific products.
        </.timeline_item>
        <.timeline_item
          title="Senior Computational Biologist · Paratus Sciences"
          icon="hero-beaker"
          badges={["Current"]}
          highlights={[
            "Drug target discovery",
            "Machine learning",
            "Phylogenetics",
            "Web technologies"
          ]}
        >
          Now, as a senior computational biologist at <.ext_link href="https://paratussciences.com">Paratus Sciences</.ext_link>,
          I am busy deploying tools and original research to accelerate our drug target discovery
          engine. By combining machine learning, evolutionary biology, web technologies, and
          phylogenetics, I am empowering my team to push the limits of our discovery pipeline.
        </.timeline_item>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="latest-posts">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-extrabold pt-8 pb-4">Latest from the blog</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        <.card
          :for={post <- @recent_posts}
          class="group flex flex-col gap-3 transition-colors hover:border-primary/30"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold leading-snug group-hover:text-primary transition-colors">
            <.link navigate={~p"/blog/#{post.id}"}>{post.title}</.link>
          </h3>
          <time
            datetime={Date.to_iso8601(post.date)}
            class="text-sm text-base-content/60"
          >
            {Calendar.strftime(post.date, "%B %d, %Y")}
          </time>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-base-content/80">{post.description}</p>
        </.card>
      </div>
      <.link
        navigate={~p"/blog"}
        class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-1 font-medium link link-primary"
      >
        Read all posts <.icon name="hero-arrow-right" class="size-4" />
      </.link>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layouts.app>
